<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sinchi Roca</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sinchi Roca was, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inca-empire">Inca</a> tradition, the second ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cusco">Cusco</a> and the son of the founder <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manco-capac">Manco Capac</a>, probably in the 13th century. Spanish chroniclers credit him with consolidating the early Inca settlement in the Cusco valley, but little is known of his reign, and his historicity is uncertain.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sinchi-roca.jpg" alt="Sinchi Roca" width="234" height="237" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Antonio de Herrera y Tordesillas (1549 - c.1625/26) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sinchi_Roca.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
